# MESSAGE: population floor, floors-as-data (ERRC-10, 2026-11-06) —
# whole-individual deletion is silent in every existence-form gate: untyping
# or deleting a gated individual fires nothing. One parametric gate replaces
# the four per-pack floor gates: it joins the arcus:PopulationFloor register
# (ontologies/arcus.ttl — 11 (class, floor) pairs, ceil(0.8 * population),
# derivation scripts/gate_mutation_court.py load_graphs() union replica,
# COUNT(DISTINCT ?s) with ISIRI guard, lane R-S7B receipt). Gates see the
# union graph, so this single arcus-pack gate guards aws/gcp/azure classes
# too. A legitimate data change that drops below a floor must re-derive and
# re-pin the floor with a new derivation date — never a silent floor drop.
# KD-G14 law: counts are DISTINCT IRIs (ISIRI guard) so the ggen union
# double-load cannot inflate them; bnode-subject classes (ResourceTop,
# ProviderConstant) are deliberately excluded — their census is the
# crosscheck leg's job (IRI-anchored), never a bare bnode count.
PREFIX arcus: <urn:arcus:>
SELECT ?class ?n WHERE {
  {
    SELECT ?cls (COUNT(DISTINCT ?s) AS ?n) WHERE {
      ?fl a arcus:PopulationFloor ; arcus:gatedClass ?cls .
      ?s a ?cls . FILTER (ISIRI(?s))
    } GROUP BY ?cls
  }
  ?fl2 a arcus:PopulationFloor ; arcus:gatedClass ?cls ; arcus:floor ?floor .
  FILTER (?n < ?floor)
  BIND (STR(?cls) AS ?class)
}
ORDER BY ?class
